From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] main: read the system ncdu.conf from all three UAPI paths
Source: no upstream commit; written for Nex against ncdu 2.9.2
Upstream: not submitted. ncdu reads one system file at /etc/ncdu.conf, so a
 distribution cannot ship a default that a boot or an administrator may
 replace. The change below adds the generic /usr/lib, /run, and /etc order,
 keeps the existing user file after those, and names no Nex path.

At startup ncdu reads /etc/ncdu.conf and then an XDG or ~/.config/ncdu/config
user file. There is no vendor or runtime tier, so a distribution cannot ship
a default configuration below /usr, and a running system cannot install a
temporary override below /run: only a persistent /etc file works.

Read /usr/lib/ncdu/ncdu.conf, then /run/ncdu.conf, then the existing
/etc/ncdu.conf, before the user file. Each file that exists overlays the
options read so far, so an administrator file still overrides a runtime
file, which still overrides a vendor file, which still overrides nothing.
--ignore-config continues to skip every one of these files.

diff -urN a/src/main.zig b/src/main.zig
--- a/src/main.zig
+++ b/src/main.zig
@@ -485,6 +485,8 @@
     };
 
     if (loadConf) {
+        tryReadArgsFile("/usr/lib/ncdu/ncdu.conf");
+        tryReadArgsFile("/run/ncdu.conf");
         tryReadArgsFile("/etc/ncdu.conf");
 
         if (std.posix.getenvZ("XDG_CONFIG_HOME")) |p| {
